They never believed that he had died in the way the sheriff said.
"They are convinced that this is contrary to logic, to the laws of physics and also to common sense," Crump said.
They believe that this should cover up what really happened in order to protect the person responsible for their son's death.
"As usual, they sent their son to school, and he came back in a body bag," he said.
