Schwarzenberg: We have early elections here in two years
TOP 09 Chairman Karel Schwarzenberg expects another early election soon.
A week after the last ones in an interview with Aktuálně.cz, he said there was no other starting point, and every government came out of the vote last Friday and Saturday is an impossible blinder.
"It can't last long," Karel Schwarzenberg said, adding that he estimates the duration of the start-up term within two years.
With the objection that voters will hardly choose in a completely different way next time, they disagree: "I think it's going to be a bit more balanced decision-making."
At the same time, the chairman of TOP 09 does not accept that his party could still lose voters in the next elections as this year (compared to 2010 it lost about 300 thousand votes).
Schwarzenberg estimates that if it became clear within two months that there would be early elections, it would strengthen Andrej Babiš's ANO 2011 movement.
Otherwise, according to Schwarzenberg, Babiš will lose.
