In 2010, authorities found a corridor about 650 meters long equipped with tracks that led from the kitchen of one house in Tijuana to two warehouses in San Diego.
Economia and the Center connect management.
For example, they offer joint advertising
Economia's new integrated newsroom in Karlín, Prague.
Economia has taken the next step for transforming the Centrum holding into its media house.
As of Friday, Economia and the Centre have joint top management.
"The unification of the organizational structure and personnel union are essential for the integration of both publishing houses into a common media house," comments the Vice-Chairman of the Board of Directors of Economy and the authorized CEO Kamil Čermák.
Čermák, who will lead the unified management, will be complemented by Andreas Demuth, Executive Director of Centrum Holdings.
Pavel Vopařil was appointed as the new joint director of the trade, to which Zuzana TylčerovÁ, the advertising director of both companies, is subordinated.
Štěpán Burda became the new head of information technology.
The joint director of the editorial offices is Vladimír Piskáček, whose team also includes Jakub Unger, the director for transformation.
Adéla Pitts was commissioned as director of marketing.
Věra Lhotská now manages a separate department of corporate communication.
The joint CFO is Karel Žalud, the management of human resources for both publishers is led by Petra Slabá.
"The new organizational structure will, among other things, allow us to come to the market with a common offer of advertising products, to better combine the creation of content of all published titles and, last but not least, to significantly streamline the company's business management," Čermák added.
Economia, owned by financier Zdeněk Bakala, entered into an agreement to buy Centrum Holdings and its Czech subsidiaries at the end of April this year.
Portfolio Centrum Holdings consists of servers Aktuálně.cz, Žena.cz, web portals, an extensive e-mail base under brands Centrum.cz and Atlas.cz and SMB agency Najisto or a portfolio of almost two dozen smaller websites.
Economia is the publisher of Hospodářské noviny, news server IHNED.cz, weekly magazines Respekt and Ekonom and a number of printed and online B2B titles.
Among Czech publishers it has long been the most successful in the sale of digital versions of its main titles.
This June, the publishing house moved to the newly built modern premises in Karlín, Prague.
CME focuses on the TV business.
They're releasing almost a quarter of people.
The CME media group will be dismissed.
By the end of the year, he wants to slim down a thousand people.
Osekat intends to focus all secondary activities and wants to focus only on his main business, television broadcasting.
The group, which owns Nova TV in the Czech Republic and also operates in Slovakia, Bulgaria, Romania, Croatia and Slovenia, employs a total of about 4 500 people.
Nearly a quarter of people lose their jobs.
The media group operates televisions in the Czech Republic, Slovakia, Bulgaria, Romania, Croatia and Slovenia.
CME includes CET 21, which holds licenses for broadcasting television stations Nova, Nova Cinema, Nova Sport, Fanda, Smíchov, Telka and Czech versions of the music station MTV.
How much the savings will affect the Czech Republic, where the group employs about 650 people, and what it will mean for the domestic TV number one TV Nova, is not yet clear.
