Both of Nova's new chief executives Christoph Mainusch and Michael Del Nin, who boarded after longtime director Adrian Sarbu, spoke during Wednesday's conference call with analysts about wanting to curtail all activities that are not directly unrelated to the TV business.
It is therefore quite likely that it will significantly reduce in particular the cost of producing its own programmes, filmmaking and production activities.
A cooling tower burned down at night in the ČKD industrial complex in Prague
There was a large-capacity reservoir in the ČKD industrial area in Prague, according to firefighters, apparently a cooling tower.
"Firefighters were leaving for the fire on Thursday before eleven o'clock in the evening, this morning they were still extinguishing the fire," Pavlína Adamcová, a spokeswoman for the Prague fire department, said in a statement.
The amount of pollutants in the air in the vicinity according to the measurements did not exceed the permitted limits.
The amount of damage and the causes of the fire are still unknown.
Approximately five dozen firefighters gradually arrived at the premises in Kolbenova Street.
"This is a large-capacity tank fire, probably a cooling tower," Adamcová said.
"There is no functioning hydrant network on the premises, so we are extinguished by means of transport lines from tanks," she added.
