He added that “this step may have caused some foreign investors to be reluctant to buy real estate in London, or that existing owners are reluctant to sell.”
Leading properties – the top 5% to 10 per cent of the housing market by price – in a rich belt that ranges from Fulham to Wimbledon, recorded an increase of 11.8% over the past year.
