Senile president and cowardly government did nothing, on the one hand they didn't believe him, on the other, they were afraid.
Gottwald's human debris was executed by his age-old co-co-comrades, as Moscow had instructed.
Ludvík Svoboda was definitively prevented by his contribution to normalization and had to dethrone him, already completely senile.
That Husák was helpless and the sick depressive old man facilitated events in November 89, but that is the only positive.
Havel was lucky that the last few years did not meet him in office, he was spared the worst.
Klaus is still a lush tennis pensioner, but many of his achievements suggest that thought processes are no longer what they used to be.
Well, now here's this.
The head of state and commander-in-chief of the armed forces looks like, and we don't know everything yet.
Fortunately, there is no external threat to the republic.
Or maybe it threatens, it's just not visible.
Then the question is whether, exceptionally (from a historical point of view), it is not good that the president is not entirely strong.
However, it is not a normal situation.
Couldn't we elect a president in this country once again to someone who's who's thinking and acceptably healthy?
Distant planets, black-and-white movies or a bit of fantasy about extraterrestrial life on earth are not topics that American saxophonist Wayne Shorter would pitch casually.
In the conception of his quartet, which on November 6 in the large hall of Prague’s Lucerna will conclude with this year’s Strings of Autumn festival, everything has to do with everything.
The scorel of the quartet of the jazz saxophonist Wayne Shorter is the current feelings of the musicians.
According to his assignment, two generations younger colleagues are supposed to play what they're experiencing right now.
They approach music as a completely improvised chamber thing and think not about harmony or rhythm, but in film paintings.
This principle, however, the newly eighty-year-old Shorter - an extraordinary composer, bearear of nine Grammys, former teammate Miles Davis and now probably the greatest living jazz saxophonist - doesn't like to explain.
He doesn't talk much about music, even though his overall outlook on life is closely related to music.
At the age of eighty, I came to the conclusion that it is best to be surprised by life.
"Too many people are planning everything, and then they're disappointed when things turn out differently," Shorter argues.
How insects from Thailand picked up sales of a Paris bar
You may be sneering at insects and you have no idea that about half a kilogram a year you eat it completely voluntarily.
For example, grinded in flour.
If you consume it consciously, then you are unambiguously trendy: it is ecological, nutritious, and you have taken care of a unique experience.
Elie Daviron, the chef and owner of Le Festin Nu's bar, was the first to include the offer of insects in Paris in early October.
The bar, inspired by William Burrough's book Naked Lunch, you'd be found in the fashionable 18th district near Montmartre widely frequented by tourists.
With fresh avocados, roasted red peppers, ginger and quail egg, guests can now bite here not only various larvae, grasshoppers or beetles, you can also taste scorpions.
Carefully and specially packaged deliveries (so as not to damage the insect's wings, do not twist their legs or damage their eyes) are sent to Daviron all the way from Thailand.
Europe is just learning to eat insects, it's common elsewhere.
The owner of a Paris bar with a groundbreaking menu lists several reasons to consume insects.
The first is the ecological benefit, because the production of insects is much less costly for our planet (in terms of finance, space and water consumption) than with traditional meat.
"In addition, insects are an excellent source of protein and omega 3 fatty acids," Daviron told Reuters.
At the same time, the young chef does not deny his profession, he simply aims to offer his customers a unique culinary experience.
According to him, the right restaurant does pleasure, a sense of sin and the atmosphere of the environment.
"I don't save the world, I'm just conveying a new experience," he explained.
Not everyone would be impressed by the idea of consuming a beetle decorated with pesto, but the reactions of customers of the Paris bar to served insects, according to the owner, are very positive.
Even skeptics are said to eventually taste, even if they start with the smallest bites, and eventually choose a scorpion.
The prices of these tasting plates range from five to nine euros.
The president of the Association of Construction Entrepreneurs in the Czech Republic Václav Matyáš: The New Green Savings should continue
Since 2008, the Czech construction industry has been struggling with a continuous decrease in the volume of orders and the lack of interest of the state to solve the issue of investment construction.
Announcing the New Green Savings programme was a positive signal for our construction industry, especially for small and medium-sized companies in individual regions.
It is a great opportunity not only for citizens, who, after the implementation of the measures, will save significant amounts for heating, but also chances for construction companies and manufacturers of building materials.
Each billion invested will bring more than 2700 newly created jobs to the state.
In terms of fiscal policy of the state there are significant leverage and multiplier effects, it is also one of the most important pro-growth measures.
Therefore, the Association of Entrepreneurs in Construction in the Czech Republic fundamentally disagrees with the resolution of the government and asks for the implementation of such steps, which would allow further continuation of the programme, so that further challenges can be announced within it.
